{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122205","id":4234111595,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc78X2pr","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122205","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122205.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122205.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122205","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122205/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122205/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122205/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/4e05a14e4c5feab5fc96502c2be4ca8ff62228b4","number":122205,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add center of mass indicator for RigidBody2D and RigidBody3D in editor","user":{"login":"jwheare","id":49224,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MjI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49224?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwheare","html_url":"https://github.com/jwheare","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwheare/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwheare/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwheare/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwheare/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwheare/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwheare/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwheare/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwheare/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwheare/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This replaces and builds on an apparently abandoned PR: #115493 by @LandonFerg\r\n\r\n> Adds a `show_center_of_mass` property to both `RigidBody2D` and `RigidBody3D` that displays an orange gizmo / crosshair indicator at the center of mass position in the editor.\r\n> \r\n> **Note** This is an editor only addition, did not implement a debug for center of mass at runtime\r\n\r\nAll commits from that PR have been squashed into the first commit. I have made 3 small additions in separate commits, and will squash them if approved.\r\n\r\n## Additional changes\r\n\r\n1. Adjusted the magenta color as per review comment by @Calinou https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115493#pullrequestreview-3877933560\r\n2. Made the gizmo always draw on top (like the transform gizmo) so that it's visible even inside solid objects (I imagine this is a common scenario) - note: only in 3D, I didn't touch or test the 2D version.\r\n3. Increased the size of the crosshair in 3D from 0.1 to 0.25 (matches e.g. Marker3D). This might be personal preference, but it was too small at the current size for my use case. I think ideally the gizmo would have a fixed screen space size, but I wasnt sure how best to achieve this without adding too much complexity in the form of a vertex shader.\r\n\r\n* *Bugsquad edit, Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/2579*","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived